mode: "100644"
text: "# Source Types — repurposing by direction\n\nDifferent sources atomize differently. This is how to handle each, so you pull the most posts\nwithout padding.\n\n---\n\n## Long-form → many short posts (the biggest multiplier)\n\nSources: a blog post, a 20-minute video, a podcast episode, a newsletter, a webinar, a talk.\n\n**Method — atomize, don't summarize:**\n1. Read/scan the whole piece and **list every atom** — each distinct insight, story, stat,\n   quote, contrarian take, or step. A solid blog post yields 5–10; a podcast can yield more.\n2. Score the atoms — which are strongest, most surprising, most standalone.\n3. Turn each strong atom into its **own** native post (per `platform-transforms.md`). One atom =\n   one post, not \"here's a summary of my blog.\"\n4. Optionally keep one post that points to the full piece (the \"hero\" link), but the atoms each\n   stand alone.\n\n**Anti-pattern:** compressing a rich 2,000-word post into one thin \"I wrote a blog, check it\nout\" post. That wastes 90% of the material.\n\n## One strong post → fan out (one → many platforms)\n\nSources: a post that did well, or a fresh single idea.\n\n**Method:** it's one atom — re-native it for each target platform (new hook, format, length,\nCTA, register). Space the posts out; vary the angle where audiences overlap. This is the default\nfan-out covered in the main flow.\n\n## One format → many formats\n\nSources: a written insight you want in more shapes.\n\n**Method:** the same atom becomes:\n- a **carousel** (break the point into slides),\n- a **Reel/Short** (hand to `reels-script`),\n- a **thread** (hand to `thread-writer`),\n- a **single post**.\nPick the formats that suit the atom and the platforms; don't force all four.\n\n## Cross-medium (video ↔ text)\n\n- **Video → text:** pull the **spoken insights, quotes, and moments** as written atoms — then\n  build native text posts. Don't dump a transcript; transcripts aren't posts.\n- **Text → video:** hand the atom to `reels-script` to build it *as a video* (hook + beats +\n  shots). Don't read the caption aloud over a static image.\n- **Long video → clips:** see `captions-and-clipping` for cutting clips; pair each clip with a\n  native caption.\n\n## Across time (recycle)\n\nEvergreen atoms can run again later, refreshed (new hook, updated example, different format) so\nit doesn't read as a literal repost. This is the time dimension — see `content-recycling` for\ncadence and refresh rules.\n\n---\n\n## Choosing how far to push it\n\n- A **hero asset** (deep blog, big video, launch) → atomize hard; it can feed weeks.\n- A **single light idea** → one or two native versions; don't manufacture filler to hit a count.\n- The test: every post must clear the quality bar on its own. If you're padding to reach a\n  number, stop — fewer, stronger posts win.\n"
